// Chords + lyrics, no staff: the chord row carries the measure barlines and the
// chords sit between them (timing-aware); the lyrics hang below the barlines.
// Chords change coarsely (at most a quarter), while the lyrics are a finer
// syllable grid — so each bar is spaced by its DENSEST row (the lyrics), and the
// chords land at their timing within. Bars 1/2 have more syllables than chords.
title "Lead sheet"
time 4/4
section Main {
  chords prog { c2 g:7 | a:m    | f2 g:7 | c1   | }
  lyrics words { Twin- kle lit- tle | star how I | won- der what | you~ | }
}
form main { Main }
score main "lead-sheet" { chords prog lyrics words }
